{
 "name": "log-menu-2",
 "description": "The structured log in the release firmware, switched by the Custom Menu row Debug Log (setting 447, patches/custom-menu-rows-2.json; default Off). log_put / log_chg / log_cnt write 16-byte records into one RAM ring per CPU (0x7E4F9000-0x7E4FD2C0) and return at once when the row is Off: from the first GUI state of a session the log does nothing more with Off, and only the start-up records are in RAM. With On, the flush task (the dormant task USRTEST_B) appends the records to C:\\\\EPM2LOG.BIN when the GUI enters a menu, playback or power-off state and neither the card nor card-looks' task is busy (stops at 4 MiB). Events: boot, firmware errors, GUI states, log_setting, the probes of log-probes (peaking, picture mode, level gauge, interval shooting, film looks, shooting callbacks), pk_stats, pk_guard and card_task (each run of card-looks' task). The code of log-core, log-probes, log-peaking-time and log-peaking-guard, placed again; the hook of the GUI state setter jumps to this T_GUI, which ends with a jump to card-looks' T_GUI. The event ids are in logs/events.json (build id 33ca8d15f4f1c877). See experiments/2026-11-18-log-menu/design.md and docs/logging.md.",
